Enables unsafe code for the crates of the ad blocker closure.

Paani builds the Brave adblock-rust engine, which depends on crates that
upstream Chromium vendors but never compiles.  Their generated BUILD.gn files
say `allow_unsafe = false`, so rustc is invoked with `-F unsafe-code` and
rejects the `unsafe` blocks in them.  The flag is turned off for exactly the
crates that //third_party/rust/adblock pulls in.
--- a/third_party/rust/adblock/v0_13/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/rust/adblock/v0_13/BUILD.gn
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@
   cargo_pkg_repository = "https://github.com/brave/adblock-rust/"
   cargo_pkg_version = "0.13.5"
 
-  allow_unsafe = false
+  allow_unsafe = true
 
   deps = [
     "//third_party/rust/addr/v0_15:lib",
--- a/third_party/rust/aho_corasick/v1/BUILD.gn
